Aarrgghh, I hate writing this shit..  oh well, here goes..


H-News is a part of the HydraTools series of /X utils,  watch out for more
cool utils from me in the near future!

H-News basically displays messages to all users when the door is run
(i put it in the BBS:Screens/BULL50.TXT file so it gets run every time
someone logs on, use the MCI command to run the door.)
The messages can be programmed to only display on a certain date,
between 2 dates and on and after a certain date.

To install it copy all the files in the BBS dir to your BBS: dir
and copy the DOORS dir to your doors: directory.



H-News is hard coded to look for the following dirs, so if you have problems
check the dirs exist.

DOORS:HydraTools/
DOORS:HydraTools/H-News/
DOORS:HydraTools/H-News/Text/
DOORS:HydraTools/H-News/Users/

also it used AEDoor.Library so have this in LIBS: or else...

The H-News program can be put anywhere, but don't forget to change the
location tooltype on the BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/NEWS.INFO file...

the News is stored in a file called "DOORS:HydraTools/H-News/Text/News.TXT"

an example is provided so take a look at this so you can understand the next
bit of this documentation...

the file is made up of sections, at the end of the file you must have
the line

:FINISH

the possible sections are defined like this..

TODAY
DD-MM-YY
:START
some boring text that will only get
displayed on the above date and no other days..
:END

(replace DD-MM-YY with a date like 30-07-94 or sommat..)

AFTER
DD-MM-YY
:START
some text that will be displayed on and after the date above, this text
will be displayed on all future logins until you remove this section
from the news file
:END

BETWEEN
DD-MM-YY
DD-MM-YY
:START
this text will get displayed on the first date and all consucutive days
until (and including) the second date.  usefull if the sysop goes on holiday
:END

those are the only possible sections to the news.txt file

*IMPORTANT*  do NOT have any blank lines between the sections or the dates or
at the top and bottom of the file or it WONT work, so after you edit the news
check it by typing NEWS at the bbs prompt to make sure it works..

the BBS:HydraTools/Users dir is used to store very small files for each of the
users on your system.  at the moment it only stores the date the user
last looked at the news, but in a future version it will contain some
preferences for each users too..

